Subject: Send a memory trim to an app the host hides although Android shows its task

DSA shows each task in its own host window, and the guest's tasks never cover each other, so a
task whose host window the user minimized, covered with other windows or left on another
virtual desktop is still a visible freeform task to Android. Its process stays in the
foreground (PROCESS_STATE_TOP), so the activity manager never sends it TRIM_MEMORY_UI_HIDDEN
as a phone's app gets when it goes to the background. The DSA agent sends the trim itself
through the shell's "am send-trim-memory", but setProcessMemoryTrimLevel refuses any level from
TRIM_MEMORY_UI_HIDDEN up for a process at PROCESS_STATE_IMPORTANT_FOREGROUND or above ("Unable
to set a background trim level on a foreground process"), so the trim never reaches the app.

The activity manager's shell command "dsa-hidden-trim" now sends it:

- "dsa-hidden-trim hidden [PACKAGE...]" sets the packages every task of which the host hides,
  replacing those before ("hidden" alone means none). The DSA agent, which holds
  MANAGE_ACTIVITY_TASKS, sets them whenever the host says which windows the user can see.
- "dsa-hidden-trim send <PROCESS> <HIDDEN|BACKGROUND>" sends the process the level, as
  setProcessMemoryTrimLevel does for a process in the background, but without waiting for the
  process to leave the foreground. Only the shell may send (the agent's trim script runs as the
  shell), only TRIM_MEMORY_UI_HIDDEN or TRIM_MEMORY_BACKGROUND, and only to a process whose
  package is set. A refusal is one line on the error output ("Error: <reason>").
- Without arguments the command prints "supported", which is how the agent and its trim script
  tell an image with this change from one without it, which answers "Unknown command".

Only the trim callback is sent. The process keeps its state and importance, its activities are
neither stopped nor hidden, and its windows do not change. "am send-trim-memory" and every app
whose package is not set behave as before, and nothing is set until the agent sets it. The set
lives in the activity manager's process, so it ends when that process does.

Applies to frameworks/base at 45034f0663f960d9ee5fb0a101a4732b71f6e2f4 (Android 16), after 0012.
---
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java
@@ -3222,6 +3222,58 @@ public class ActivityManagerService extends IActivityManager.Stub
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * DSA: the packages every task of which the host hides from the user (all its windows
+     * minimized, covered by other windows or on another virtual desktop), as the DSA agent last
+     * set them with the shell command "dsa-hidden-trim hidden". Android still counts such a
+     * task as visible, since its freeform window stays on the guest's display, so its process
+     * stays in the foreground and setProcessMemoryTrimLevel refuses it a background trim level.
+     * The set is replaced, never changed in place.
+     */
+    volatile java.util.Set<String> mDsaHiddenPackages = java.util.Collections.emptySet();
+
+    /**
+     * DSA: sends a process of a package the host hides a background trim level (HIDDEN or
+     * BACKGROUND), as setProcessMemoryTrimLevel sends one to a process in the background. As
+     * there, only the shell may ask; and only for a process whose package is in
+     * mDsaHiddenPackages, for which it does not wait for the process to leave the foreground,
+     * which the process of a task Android shows never does. Nothing else changes: the process
+     * keeps its state and importance, and its activities are neither stopped nor hidden.
+     */
+    boolean dsaSetHiddenProcessMemoryTrimLevel(String process, @UserIdInt int userId, int level)
+            throws RemoteException {
+        if (!isCallerShell()) {
+            throw new SecurityException("Only shell can call it");
+        }
+        if (level < ComponentCallbacks2.TRIM_MEMORY_UI_HIDDEN) {
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Only a background trim level is sent this way");
+        }
+        synchronized (this) {
+            final ProcessRecord app = findProcessLOSP(process, userId,
+                    "dsaSetHiddenProcessMemoryTrimLevel");
+            if (app == null) {
+                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unknown process: " + process);
+            }
+            final IApplicationThread thread = app.getThread();
+            if (thread == null) {
+                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Process has no app thread");
+            }
+            if (app.info == null || !mDsaHiddenPackages.contains(app.info.packageName)) {
+                throw new IllegalArgumentException(
+                        "The host has not hidden the tasks of " + process);
+            }
+            if (app.mProfile.getTrimMemoryLevel() >= level) {
+                throw new IllegalArgumentException(
+                        "Unable to set a higher trim level than current level");
+            }
+            thread.scheduleTrimMemory(level);
+            synchronized (mProcLock) {
+                app.mProfile.setTrimMemoryLevel(level);
+            }
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+
